Reset the output resampler phase together with its sample queue.

A fractional position left by drift compensation survived SoundEngine::reset,
so a reset stream interpolated its first samples and left one frame buffered
instead of matching a fresh engine. Keep the reset under the output mutex.
The standalone sound regression reproduces the old failure after a 1.05x drain
and verifies sample/count equality after reset. No gameplay FPS or audio-dropout
improvement is claimed.

diff --git a/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp b/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp
--- a/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp
+++ b/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
         {
             std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m_outputMutex);
             m_output.clear();
+            m_resamplePhase = 0.0;
         }
         m_lastCycle = 0;
         m_targetCycle = 0;
